# 6. Expansion Revenue Strategy

- **Upsell triggers**: What behavior signals a user is ready for a higher tier?
- **Cross-sell opportunities**: Add-ons, integrations, professional services
- **Seat expansion**: How to encourage team adoption (sharing features, team dashboards)
- **Usage-based expansion**: How usage growth naturally increases revenue
- **Annual conversion**: Tactics to move monthly subscribers to annual plans
- **Net revenue retention target**: >100% (expansion > churn) — realistic timeline to achieve this

# 7. Pricing Risks & Sensitivities

| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|--------|------------|
| Price too high → low conversion | Revenue miss | A/B test pricing, offer extended trials |
| Price too low → not sustainable | Cash flow issues | Plan price increase after PMF, grandfather early users |
| Competitor undercuts | User migration | Differentiate on value, not price |
| Free tier too generous | No upgrade incentive | Monitor free-to-paid funnel, adjust limits |
| Churn spike at renewal | Revenue volatility | Annual discounts, engagement before renewal |

# 8. Implementation Recommendations

- **Payment processor**: Stripe / Paddle / LemonSqueezy — recommendation with rationale (tax handling, subscription management, global support)
- **Billing infrastructure**: What to build vs what the payment processor handles
- **Price change strategy**: How to test and implement price changes without alienating existing users
- **Discount policy**: When to offer discounts (annual plans, student/nonprofit, startups), when to avoid them
- **Pricing page design**: Key principles for an effective pricing page (social proof, feature comparison, FAQ)

