CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:
- All pricing recommendations must be grounded in the competitive data. Don't price in a vacuum.
- Revenue projections must show explicit assumptions — they're only useful if someone can challenge the inputs.
- Consider the target audience's willingness to pay. A $50/mo B2C app for college students is very different from a $500/mo B2B tool.
- The free-to-paid boundary is the most important pricing decision. Spend the most thought here.
- Include actual dollar amounts, not ranges. You can provide scenarios but make a clear recommendation.

